Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 02:07:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(tts/pocket): keep a sentence whole when it fits the
 KV cache, and never generate past the cache

- chunkTextWithMetadata takes maxWholeSentenceTokens: a sentence over maxTokensPerChunk stays whole when it is within that limit, as the reference split_into_best_sentences does; longer sentences are still cut
- maxWholeSentenceTokens(voiceSlots:) derives the limit from kvCacheMaxLen, the voice's cache footprint, cacheReserveSlots and generationFramesPerTokenBudget (4 slots of audio per text token; 75 tokens for a 125-frame voice)
- generationStepLimit caps all four generation loops at the slots left in the cache; the cache write index wraps, so a step past the last slot overwrites the voice prompt
- PocketTtsVoiceData.cacheSlots reports the voice's footprint for shipped and cloned voices
- Local experiment resting on an assumed speaking rate; a larger cache export would remove the assumption
